<title>HONG KONG: S&amp;P buys stake in India CRISIL.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P buys stake in India CRISIL.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rating agency Standard &amp; Poor's (S&amp;P) said on Thursday it has bought a 9.6 percent stake in Credit Rating Information Services of India Ltd (CRISIL).</p>
<p>S&amp;P and CRISIL formed a strategic business alliance in 1996, providing for analytical and business development cooperation, S&amp;P said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The Indian marketplace offers both organisations considerable opportunities in the traditional ratings business,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The deal, announced in May, was sealed after approval from the Reserve Bank of India, it said.</p>
<p>The terms of the agreement were not disclosed.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
